<http://www.semanticweb.org/tobia/ontologies/2025/1/Vocabulary_2025_03_13> rdf:type owl:Ontology .
:UrologyEmergency rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
                  :ActivityDescription "CIRS Case number: 270499		Description: An inpatient received emergency medical intervention in a specialised outpatient clinic during the night. The patient was then transferred to a monitoring ward and later brought back to the original peripheral ward by a nurse. On the ward, the nurse discovered that the extension set of the intravenous catheter (IVC) still contained residues of a cloudy-coloured medication (sedative). In addition, the intravenous catheter was covered by a gauze bandage. As a result, there was a risk that someone could rinse the IVC without checking the contents and inadvertently administer the remaining medication in the bolus to the patient." ;
                  :ActivityName "Before Debriefing: Compliance with the specifications for handling intravenous catheters" .

